## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of synchronization primitives and memory ordering in a toy OS context.

## Key Concepts

- Barrier reuse via a generation counter
- Race-free wakeups with a condition variable analogue
- Memory visibility and minimal locking
- Testing for progress and fairness under contention

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct {
  int count;
  int needed;
  int gen;
  pthread_mutex_t m;
  pthread_cond_t cv;
} barrier_t;

void barrier_init(barrier_t *b, int n) {
  b->count = 0;
  b->needed = n;
  b->gen = 0;
  pthread_mutex_init(&b->m, NULL);
  pthread_cond_init(&b->cv, NULL);
}

void barrier_wait(barrier_t *b) {
  pthread_mutex_lock(&b->m);
  int g = b->gen;
  if (++b->count == b->needed) {
    b->count = 0;
    b->gen++;
    pthread_cond_broadcast(&b->cv);
  } else {
    while (b->gen == g) {
      pthread_cond_wait(&b->cv, &b->m);
    }
  }
  pthread_mutex_unlock(&b->m);
}
```

